  <section class="ab-thesis" aria-labelledby="ab-thesis-title">
    <span>01 / THE RECURRING PROBLEM</span>
    <h2 id="ab-thesis-title">A result becomes trusted.<br />Its construction disappears.</h2>
    <div>
      <p>The raw rural credit gap looked like a fact about rural markets. In a descriptive, noncausal comparison, the coefficient falls from −0.262 to −0.047 after adding intermediary identity. Static geographic distance looks harmless until a canal closes, a drought changes a route, or a corridor comes under attack.</p>
      <p>I keep returning to that moment. What did the measure assume? Which comparison produced the estimate? What changes when the assumption moves? I build the model, figure, viewer, or lesson that lets another person answer those questions directly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ab-modes" aria-labelledby="ab-modes-title">
    <header><span>02 / ONE PRACTICE · THREE MODES</span><h2 id="ab-modes-title">The research, teaching,<br />and code correct one another.</h2><p>Research keeps the lesson honest. Teaching exposes the sentence that still does not work. Building turns the recurring explanation into a public object.</p></header>
    <div>
      <article><span>R / 01</span><strong>8,024</strong><h3>Projects changed the interpretation.</h3><p>The descriptive NMTC decomposition motivates evaluating intermediary allocation while leaving the mechanism unresolved.</p><a href="/research">Open the research record →</a></article>
      <article><span>T / 02</span><strong>1,003</strong><h3>Public tutoring hours sharpened the diagnosis.</h3><p>High school, undergraduate, MBA, graduate, research, and professional work reveal the first broken link at different scales. The public Wyzant snapshot is current through August 2026.</p><a href="/teaching">Open the teaching record →</a></article>
      <article><span>B / 03</span><strong>OPEN</strong><h3>Tools kept the explanation running.</h3><p>Viewers, observatories, laboratories, atlases, and research pipelines let a visitor change the input and inspect what follows.</p><a href="/projects">Open the tools →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

